        "url": "https://www.haze.gov.sg/"
       }
      ],
      "text": "**I’d skip an outdoor workout in Jurong right now.** NEA’s latest update for **Saturday, October 17** reported Singapore’s 1-hour PM2.5 at **106–198 µg/m³**, ranging from elevated to high; it advises healthy people to **avoid strenuous outdoor activity when readings are high**. NEA also forecast unhealthy to very unhealthy air for October 18. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026))\n\nChoose an indoor workout instead, especially if you have asthma or a heart or lung condition. For any brief outdoor activity, check the latest West-region PM2.5 in NEA’s **myENV** app first—the reading can change. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
